WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.474 --> 00:00:12.682
Posing an arm joint by joint is slow. With inverse kinematics you drag the hand, and the shoulder and elbow follow.

2
00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:16.090
Add an R15 rig and select the right hand.

3
00:00:17.532 --> 00:00:23.964
Press T for the IK tool. The gizmo becomes a move handle, and the whole arm is the chain.

4
00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:31.161
Drag the hand up and forward. The elbow bends and the shoulder turns on their own, and the pose is keyed.

5
00:00:31.542 --> 00:00:38.934
It works the same for feet. Select the left foot, press T, and lift it. The knee bends the way a knee should.

6
00:00:39.314 --> 00:00:46.826
Go to frame 24 and bring both back down. Two keys, and the arm and leg travel on natural arcs.

7
00:00:47.206 --> 00:00:50.590
Space plays it. No joint was rotated by hand.

8
00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:58.380
By default the IK chain reaches three joints up. You can change that from the command palette under IK chain length.

9
00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:05.244
IK, onion skin, and the curve editor are all in the free app. Nothing here needs a key.

